WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Xu Xiake loved to travel from a young age, walking all over China with a wooden staff and a notebook.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.600
His mother stood at the gate waving, watching him head toward the distant mountain road.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.400
He climbed high famous mountains, saw magnificent waterfalls, and ventured deep into caves to explore.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:20.800
The waterfall plunged straight down from above, its spray splashing like pearls.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:28.400
Xu Xiake traveled along the great river, carefully observing its direction to see where the water flowed.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.400
The small boat moved slowly forward between green mountains and clear waters, the scenery as beautiful as a painting.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:39.000
Every night, no matter how tired he was, he carefully wrote the mountains, rivers, and things he had seen into his notebook.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:46.000
The moon rose outside the window; only after writing the last line did he blow out the lamp and rest.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:51.800
He traveled for more than thirty years, never stopping, going to many places no one else had ever been.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:57.200
His notes were later compiled into The Travels of Xu Xiake, a precious work of geography and literature.
